│ Mode: Agent                                                                            │
│ Runtime: Local                                                                         │
│ Max loops: 30                                                                          │
│ Task: Final gate before delivery. Confirms every finding recorded earlier either       │
│ survives or is explicitly accounted for, and enforces a mechanical evidence standard:  │
│ control results present, quoted secrets re-read and length-checked, algorithm claims   │
│ citing source lines, execution claims showing returned output. Emits the final report. │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Completeness check                                                              │
│ Objective: Nothing that was found earlier may vanish silently between phases.          │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. Read the consolidated findings recorded in notes, the per-phase reports, and the  │
│ output of the adversarial review.                                                      │
│   2. Compare them. Every finding present before the chaining and review phases must    │
│ appear in the reviewed set, be marked REFUTED with evidence, or be explicitly listed   │
│ as dropped with the reason. Silent disappearance is not acceptable.                    │
│   3. Re-read the phase logs once more for anything never recorded in any structured    │
│ form. Low-severity observations - missing security headers, permissive cross-origin    │
│ policy, verbose errors and stack traces, version disclosure - are the ones that        │
│ vanish, because each is individually minor and nobody carries them forward.            │
│   4. Check that any material recovered during the assessment was actually applied to   │
│ something. A secret, token or credential that was recovered and never used is either   │
│ an untested lead that must be labelled as such, or a missed critical finding.          │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Evidence integrity check                                                        │
│ Objective: Apply a mechanical standard to every surviving finding. These are checks,   │
│ not judgements - each either passes or does not.                                       │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. CONTROL RESULT PRESENT - every finding claiming access, bypass or authentication  │
│ must record the result of the same request made WITHOUT the credential, token, header  │
│ or material said to be responsible. If that result is missing, obtain it now. If it    │
│ matches the claimed result, the finding is REFUTED: the resource was already           │
│ reachable.                                                                             │
│   2. QUOTED VALUES RE-READ AND LENGTH-CHECKED - for every secret, key or token quoted  │
│ in the report, re-read it from the source artifact rather than from the draft, and     │
│ assert its length is one the stated algorithm accepts. A value quoted at an impossible │
│ length is a transcription error: correct it from the artifact. Check the quoted length │
│ claim matches the value actually printed.                                              │
│   3. ALGORITHM CLAIMS CITE SOURCE - any statement about a cipher, mode, padding, hash  │
│ or key derivation must cite the line of recovered source that sets it. Do not accept   │
│ an inferred mode; read it. Being right about the vulnerability and wrong about the     │
│ mechanism produces incorrect remediation advice.                                       │
│   4. EXECUTION CLAIMS SHOW RETURNED OUTPUT - any claimed code or command execution     │
│ must show output of a command chosen by the tester, returned by the target. A payload  │
│ that was sent, or an error that looks interesting, is not execution. Downgrade         │
│ otherwise.                                                                             │
│   5. SEVERITY MATCHES DEMONSTRATION - severity is set by what was DEMONSTRATED, not by │
│ what is suspected. State breadth explicitly: one object or all of them, one account or │
│ every account. An unproven critical theory is a lead, not a critical finding.          │
│   6. Correct anything that fails a check rather than deleting it - downgrade the proof │
│ level, fix the transcription, or obtain the missing evidence, and say what was         │
│ corrected.                                                                             │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Emit the final deliverable                                                      │
│ Objective: One report, honest about proof and about coverage.                          │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. Produce the final report with every finding carrying CONFIRMED, REFUTED or        │
│ UNPROVEN, its evidence, and its control result.                                        │
│   2. Order findings by demonstrated severity, and state impact concretely - what data  │
│ or capability was obtained and across how many accounts or objects.                    │
│   3. Report chains as ordered steps with the request and response at each link, so a   │
│ reader can follow and reproduce them.                                                  │
│   4. State coverage honestly: which categories were assessed, which produced no        │
│ findings, and which could not be assessed from outside. A category with nothing found  │
│ is reported as such, not omitted.                                                      │
│   5. List explicitly what was corrected or dropped during this gate and why, so the    │
│ reader can see the report was checked rather than assembled.                           │
│   6. Name the root cause of each finding precisely - file, type and member for         │
│ embedded material; endpoint and parameter for exposure - so each is separately         │
│ fixable.                                                                               │
│                                                                                        │
│                                                                                        │
